        {
          "id": 647879938,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "It became somewhat strange because the btcommon_le_channel_map_handle dissector is re-used between the connection indication and the sync info header. The difference is that the three bits in the connection indication is reserved, while the three bits are used for the CA field in the sync info header.\nThat is why the btcommon_le_channel_map_handle dissector is returning the offset to the reserved bits in reserved_offset (but as offset into the channel_map field) which is why offset + reserved_offset = CA field.\n\nProviding the pointer to reserved_offset is also what prevents the btcommon_le_channel_map_handle dissector from marking these bits as reserved.\n\nLet me know if you think there is a better way to do this.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7680107,
            "username": "joerchan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Joakim Andersson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1599350a780a1aac15a35fe721ac69109f2a1d1869d571d95cf17243bfeef622?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/joerchan"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-08-10T18:55:36.837Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-08-10T18:55:36.837Z",
